CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ operator\[\] result: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
Invariant check failed
--
`sizeof(t[0])' parses as the type `t[0]' first; when `t' named an object
the front end built an array index expression, whose constructor requires
an array operand, and crashed for a class object.
